// SPEED ZONE — COWBELL — one song: what it plays, how it is arranged, how it sounds.
//
// SPEED ZONE as drift phonk at 130 — a game alternate of speed, selectable from the dev
// menu (GAME ALTERNATES) and on the desk. Nothing replaces the live song.
// 
// Drift phonk's signature is a TR-808 cowbell played as a melody, and THE RIFF (E5 . .
// B4 . E5 . G5 . E5 . B4 . A4 . B4 — what the player hears every lap) was always a
// sixteenth-note cowbell line: here it is one, on a song-local voice built the 808's way
// (two squares at 540:800 through a bandpass that tracks the key). Under it a distorted
// 808 sliding between the cabinet's own bass roots, a clipped kick, the clap on three.
// THE SYNTH LEAD (speed.js lead4, HORIZON LINES' melody) is an eerie ice bell an octave
// up in the first drop and is sung by a talk-box lead in the second. Both drops keep
// the cabinet's gear changes: E, A, B minor.
// 
//   1–4    intro — the cowbell riff alone in a big room, choir (the cabinet-screen loop)
//   5–12   DROP — half-time phonk in E minor; the ice bell's synth lead from bar 9
//   13–20  the gears — A minor, B minor, the synth lead following
//   21–28  slow-mo drift — the riff at half speed, the 808 gliding; the build
//   29–44  DROP TWO — four on the floor, pumping 808, cowbell doubled, talk box on the
//          synth lead: a, b, A minor, B minor
//   45–48  outro — half-time into the loop (bar 5)
// 
// Home key E minor (the coyote howl and the wink are E minor, baked at the song's
// tempo); the first drop is bar 5, the moment the stage starts.
// 
// 48 bars at 130, 89 s. Written by work/local/_speed-remix-cowbell.mjs through
// work/local/_remix-lib.mjs; re-running it rewrites this file.
//
